  "body": "When the `Url::host` setter is invoked for an URL in the `file` scheme, the parser starts in the \"host state\" (not the \"file host state\") so the URL can (per spec) end up with a non-null port number, which otherwise never happens.\n\nIn this test case: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=3927 Firefox doesn’t change the URL at all, Chromium changes the host but not the port number.\n",
